FILE: app/src/play-again.ts
```ts
import { playAnimation, stopAnimation } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import type { AnimationGroup } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function playAgain(group: AnimationGroup): void {
    stopAnimation(group);
    playAnimation(group);
}
```

I created `src/play-again.ts` with a `playAgain` function that calls `stopAnimation` (which resets `currentTime` to the group's start) followed by `playAnimation` (which clears the stop and begins playing). This works for both property groups (which set `isPlaying` to false at the end) and glTF groups (which keep `isPlaying` true but stay clamped at the end), as confirmed by notes 4, 7, 27, 39, and 53. I'm confident in this; nothing was uncertain.
